==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|*squalen}} {{q|not recorded}} and {{m|enm|squelen|t=to cry, scream, squall}}, from {{der|en|non|skvala|t=to cry out}}. Cognate with {{cog|sv|skvala|t=to gush, pour down}}, {{cog|no|skval|t=sudden rush of water}}. The noun is probably from the verb.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɔːl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|meteorology}} A [[squall line]], multicell line, or part of a squall line.
# {{lb|en|often|nautical}} A sudden [[storm]], as found in a squall line.
# A loud cry or wail.

